# SABOTAGE: MG-22 (ADR-049 mutation ledger) — `Samen.Policy.SameOrgFk.target_org_id/2`'s
# `:no_data_layer` bail-out is NARROWED from `or` to `and`, so it fires only when BOTH the
# repo AND the table are missing. A destination with one but not the other no longer fails
# closed: execution falls through to the query arm, which interpolates the missing table
# into SQL or calls `query/2` on `nil`. The guard stops REFUSING what it cannot verify and
# starts crashing on it instead — the fail-closed contract replaced by an incident.
#
# Invisible to every shipped resource: no samen_core resource has a table without a repo, so
# `or` never has to be an `or`. That is why the named red builds a destination that has a
# real `cpy_company` table and a function repo that never resolves, and asserts the
# exactly-one-is-nil precondition before exercising the guard — and why it asserts the
# `:no_data_layer` message specifically, not merely that the write was refused.
#
# Flips the named MG-22 red. MG-21's red and its cross-org control stay green: this patch
# touches ONE line, leaving the repo fallback chain above it exactly as it is.
#
# One boolean operator. Touches policy/same_org_fk.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/same_org_fk_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-22: a target with a table but NO resolvable repo fails CLOSED with :no_data_layer
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Policy.SameOrgFk do
     org_id_source = attribute_source(dest, :org_id)
 
     cond do
-      is_nil(repo) or is_nil(table) ->
+      is_nil(repo) and is_nil(table) ->
         {:error, :no_data_layer}
 
       is_nil(org_id_source) ->
